# Changelog

All notable changes to the Siyakhana Legal Advice Centre website project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/), and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

---

# Changelog

## [Unreleased]

### Planned

- Replace placeholder business contact details with confirmed information.
- Connect forms to a secure server-side form service when backend development is allowed.
- Add CSS styling during the styling phase of the project.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-07-28

### Added
- **2026-07-28-Initial HTML structure for five complete pages: Home, About, Services, Inquiry, and Contact.
- **2026-07-30-Responsive viewport metadata and semantic accessibility structure.
- **2026-08-04- Inquiry, quotation, and room-booking request form with HTML validation.
- **2026-08-06-Service descriptions for room accommodation, conference facilities, corporate catering, and local tour guidance.
- **2026-08-11-Complete business operating-hours table on contact page.
- **2026-08-13-Final project documentation set up, testing, publishing and version control and ReadMe files for release.


## [1.1.0] – 2026-09-17

### Added
- Complete set of organisation images (logo, homepage illustrations, service images)
- Proper image references across all pages
- Clean project structure with dedicated `Images/` folder

### Fixed
- Broken image paths that prevented images from displaying
- Missing image files in the final project package

---

## [1.0.0] – 2026-09-17

### Added
- Clean, fully functional multi-page website
- Responsive design (mobile, tablet, and desktop)
- Consistent header and navigation on every page
- Professional footer with contact details and social media icons
- Fixed “Chat with Siyakhana Legal” button
- Google Maps embed on the Contact page
- Enquiry form with personal details and consultation booking options
- Contact form with location and enquiry type selectors
- Single consolidated CSS file using CSS variables
- Project README documentation

### Changed
- Completely rebuilt all HTML pages from the original messy code
- Reorganised and cleaned the entire CSS (removed duplicated and conflicting styles)
- Standardised colour scheme, typography, and spacing across the site
- Improved accessibility (ARIA labels, proper heading structure, focus states)

### Fixed
- Multiple nested and duplicated `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html>`, and `<body>` tags
- Broken and incomplete header brand links
- Incorrect and inconsistent relative file paths
- Overlapping and conflicting CSS rules
- Missing closing tags and structural errors
- Non-functional layout on smaller screens

### Removed
- All duplicated footer code that was pasted into every page
- Unused and conflicting style blocks
- Placeholder / broken social media links structure (cleaned and standardised)

---

## Summary of Major Improvements

| Area              | Before                              | After                                      |
|-------------------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| HTML Structure    | Broken, nested, duplicated tags     | Clean, valid, single-document pages        |
| CSS               | Multiple conflicting style blocks   | One organised stylesheet with variables    |
| Responsiveness    | Limited / inconsistent              | Fully responsive on all screen sizes       |
| Images            | Missing / broken paths              | All images included and correctly linked   |
| Navigation        | Inconsistent across pages           | Consistent header on every page            |
| Footer            | Duplicated and messy                | Single clean footer design                 |
| Forms             | Incomplete structure                | Properly structured and styled forms       |

